1) Why do we even need an Embedding Layer?"
"Neural networks work only with numerical input, so text must be converted into numbers before training.
Traditional techniques like One-Hot Encoding, Bag of Words, and TF-IDF do this, but they create large,
sparse vectors and cannot capture the meaning or order of words. That is why we use an Embedding Layer."

Q: Why is Embedding critical for RNN?
"Without embeddings, RNN only sees meaningless numbers like one-hot vectors or word indexes,
which carry no information about meaning. An embedding layer converts each word into a small dense vector
that captures semantic meaning, so similar words like 'good' and 'great' have similar vectors.
This gives the RNN meaningful input and helps it learn context better.

Embedding layer converts words (integers) → into dense vectors (numbers)